@page "/toolbar-page"

<PageTitle>Toolbar</PageTitle>

<h1>Toolbar</h1>

<p>
    The <code>WinOldToolbar</code> and <code>WinOldToolbarButton</code> components provide an adaptive
    button bar, available across all supported visual styles, with two configurable overflow behaviors.
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Wrap</strong> (default): the classic Win32 rebar behavior: the bar spans multiple lines when it runs out of room, labels always stay visible.</li>
    <li><strong>Collapse</strong> : the Excel Online / Office ribbon behavior: the bar stays on a single line and buttons drop their text label (icon + tooltip only) one at a time, starting from the rightmost, as the bar's own measured width shrinks — fully automatic.</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <code>WinOldToolbarButton</code> also supports a <strong>Flat</strong> look (no background/border until hovered or
    pressed, the classic IE4/Office97 toolbar style), and <code>WinOldToolbarSeparator</code> draws a thin vertical
    divider to group buttons within a bar.
</p>


<h2>Examples by Style</h2>

<div style="display:flex; flex-direction: row; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-start;">

    <div style="flex:1 1 calc(50% - 20px); min-width:280px;">
        <h7>Windows 98</h7>
        <WinOldToolbar Appearance="Appearance.Win98" Mode="ToolbarOverflowMode.Collapse">
            <WinOldToolbarButton Label="New"   IconCssClass="bi bi-file-earmark"  OnClick="@(() => DoAction("New"))" />
            <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Open"  IconCssClass="bi bi-folder2-open"  OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Open"))" />
            <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Save"         OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Save"))" >
                <IconTemplate><img src="img/toolbar/save-16x16.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></IconTemplate>
            </WinOldToolbarButton>
            <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Cut"   IconCssClass="bi bi-scissors"      OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Cut"))" />
            <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Copy"  IconCssClass="bi bi-copy"          OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Copy"))" />
            <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Paste" IconCssClass="bi bi-clipboard"     OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Paste"))" />
            <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Print" IconCssClass="bi bi-printer"      Disabled />
        </WinOldToolbar>
    </div>

