<h2>Colored icons</h2>

<p>
    Use <code>IconTemplate</code> with an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> for full-color icons instead of a monochrome icon
    font. Drop your own PNGs into <code>wwwroot/img/toolbar/</code> (see the README in that folder) . This example
    references filenames that aren't included in the repo, so you'll see broken-image placeholders until you add them.
</p>

<WinOldToolbar Appearance="Appearance.WinXP" Flat="true">
    <WinOldToolbarButton IconOnly="true" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("New"))">
        <IconTemplate><img src="img/toolbar/new.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></IconTemplate>
    </WinOldToolbarButton>
    <WinOldToolbarButton IconOnly="true" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Open"))">
        <IconTemplate><img src="img/toolbar/open.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></IconTemplate>
    </WinOldToolbarButton>
    <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Save" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Save"))">
        <IconTemplate><img src="img/toolbar/save-16x16.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></IconTemplate>
    </WinOldToolbarButton>
    <WinOldToolbarSeparator />
    <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Cut" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Cut"))">
        <IconTemplate><img src="img/toolbar/cut.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></IconTemplate>
    </WinOldToolbarButton>
    <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Copy" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Copy"))">
        <IconTemplate><img src="img/toolbar/copy.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></IconTemplate>
    </WinOldToolbarButton>
    <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Paste" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Paste"))">
        <IconTemplate><img src="img/toolbar/paste.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></IconTemplate>
    </WinOldToolbarButton>
</WinOldToolbar>

<h2>Collapse mode</h2>

<p>As the box below is narrowed, buttons drop their text label one at a time — starting from the rightmost — until the row fits, keeping only the icon + native tooltip on each collapsed button. Widen it back and labels reappear in the same order. This example has enough buttons that a few are already collapsed at the default width.</p>

<p>
    If the box gets so narrow that even every button in icon-only form still doesn't fit, the bar falls back to a
    horizontal scrollbar instead of shrinking further. A button already forced icon-only via its own or the toolbar's
    <code>IconOnly="true"</code> is skipped by the collapse logic — it has nothing left to give up, so it's left alone.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">
    <strong>Tip :</strong> drag the bottom-right corner of the dashed boxes below to resize them and see each mode react live.
</div>

<div style="resize:horizontal; overflow:auto; border:1px dashed #999; padding:8px; min-width:200px; max-width:100%; width:700px;">
    <WinOldToolbar Appearance="Appearance.Win10" Mode="ToolbarOverflowMode.Collapse">
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="New"   IconCssClass="bi bi-file-earmark"  OnClick="@(() => DoAction("New"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Open"  IconCssClass="bi bi-folder2-open"  OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Open"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Save"  IconCssClass="bi bi-floppy"        OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Save"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Undo"  IconCssClass="bi bi-arrow-counterclockwise" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Undo"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Redo"  IconCssClass="bi bi-arrow-clockwise" OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Redo"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Cut"   IconCssClass="bi bi-scissors"      OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Cut"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Copy"  IconCssClass="bi bi-copy"          OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Copy"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Paste" IconCssClass="bi bi-clipboard"     OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Paste"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Find"  IconCssClass="bi bi-search"        OnClick="@(() => DoAction("Find"))" />
        <WinOldToolbarButton Label="Print" IconCssClass="bi bi-printer"      Disabled />
    </WinOldToolbar>
</div>

